ric homes in Lyons and Bordeaux. These shutters resemble standard doors, except the bottom half features a lattice or trellis pattern, providing a sturdy grip. These particular shutters measure at least three and a half feet wide. When we viewed them from the rear, they were both partially open, positioned at right angles to the wall. It is likely the police inspected the back of the building, but if they viewed these ferrades edge-on, they would have failed to notice their significant width or neglected to consider its importance. Having convinced themselves that no exit was possible from this side, they would have conducted only a superficial inspection."
